Option 2: Self-Hosted RAG Solution
Build a custom RAG pipeline using open-source components and existing infrastructure.

Technology Options:

Vector Database: Elasticsearch k-NN (existing cluster), Milvus, Weaviate, Qdrant

Embedding Models: Sentence-Transformers, text-embedding-005 via API

Orchestration: LangChain, Haystack, LlamaIndex

Document Processing: PyPDF, Unstructured, custom chunking logic

Pros
Full Control: Customize every aspect of chunking, embedding, retrieval

Data Sovereignty: Keep all data in Mumbai (ap-south-1)

Lower Operational Cost: Only compute/storage costs, no managed service fees

No Vendor Lock-in: Can switch components or migrate freely

Transparency: Complete visibility into retrieval process

Optimization Flexibility: Fine-tune for specific use case requirements

Existing Infrastructure: Leverage current Elasticsearch cluster (10.1.2.175:9200)

Integration Freedom: Works with any LLM provider (Gemini, Claude, GPT)

Cons
Higher Implementation Effort: Significantly more code to write and test

Maintenance Burden: Ongoing updates, monitoring, scaling responsibility

Operational Overhead: Monitoring, alerting, incident response needed

Quality Risk: Self-built retrieval may not match managed service quality

Time-to-Market: Takes longer to implement and stabilize

Scaling Complexity: Manual capacity planning and optimization

Feature Gap: May lack advanced features like query rewriting, reranking

 

