Decision
Selected Option: Option 1 - Fully Managed RAG Service
Specific Implementation: Vertex AI RAG Engine (Google Cloud)

Reasoning
Time-to-Market Priority: Business needs SOP compliance capabilities quickly to remain competitive

Resource Constraints: Keeps implementation scope focused on RAG integration rather than expanding to include vector database operations and maintenance

Gemini Integration: Vertex AI RAG Engine provides native integration with our existing Gemini 2.5 Flash models

Quality Assurance: Google's proven retrieval algorithms reduce risk of poor accuracy in critical compliance use case

Operational Excellence: Allows team to focus on business logic rather than vector search optimization

Scalability Confidence: Auto-scaling ensures system works from 10 to 1000 tenants without re-architecture

Feature Velocity: Advanced capabilities (query rewriting, reranking) available immediately without development

Trade-offs to be Accepted
Regional Constraint:

Vertex AI RAG Engine requires us-east4 region (Virginia, USA)

Data stored outside India: Requires legal/compliance review

Additional latency: +200-400ms per query (Mumbai → Virginia → Mumbai)

Mitigation: Document data flow in privacy policies; offer alternative for customers requiring India-only data

Cost Impact:

Estimated $150-300/month for managed service

Higher than self-hosted but justified by reduced engineering overhead

Mitigation: Set usage alerts and implement rate limiting per tenant

Vendor Lock-in:

Tight coupling to Google Cloud ecosystem

Migration to alternative would require significant refactoring

Mitigation: Design abstraction layer in code to isolate RAG implementation details

 

 

